<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Udai Singh of Kaithal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1843</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhai Udai Singh was the last ruler of Kaithal, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> chiefship of the Cis-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutlej-river">Sutlej</a> region in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a> that had accepted British protection in 1809. When he died childless in 1843, the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> annexed most of the state as a lapsed territory and put down resistance by its supporters. Kaithal then became a British district headquarters.</p></div>
